  "text_md": "## Good Gradings of Generalized Incidence Rings\n\nKenneth L Price\n\nUniversity of Wisconsin Oshkosh October 11, 2018\n\n## Abstract\n\nThis inquiry is based on both the construction of generalized incidence due to Gene Abrams and the construction of group gradings of incidence algebras due to Molli Jones. We provide conditions for a generalized incidence ring to be graded isomorphic to a subring of an incidence ring over preorder . We also extend Jones's construction to group gradings for incidence algebras over preorders with crosscuts of length one Or rings good good two.\n\n## 1 Overview\n\nUnless otherwise stated we use multiplicative notation for all semigroup, monoid, or group operations and the identity is denoted by 1.\n\nSuppose G is semigroup and S is a which does not necessarily contain multiplicative identity. We say S is a G-graded if there is direct sum ring ring",
